.vexus/
# Explicit belt-and-suspenders for eval fixture corpora: index artifacts
# from ad-hoc `vexus index eval/corpora/...` runs must never be committed
# (the `.vexus/` pattern above already covers this at any depth, but the
# eval fixtures get their own line since it's load-bearing for that gate).
eval/**/.vexus/
# Written by `vexus-eval run` on every invocation (local + CI eval-gate) —
# a fresh, regeneratable artifact, not ground truth (unlike
# eval/baseline-mock.json, which is committed deliberately).
eval/last-run.json
# Appended to by `vexus-eval perf` on every invocation (local + the CI perf
# advisory job) — a running log of raw timings, not a committed artifact;
# bench/budgets.json (the thresholds those timings are compared against) IS
# committed.
bench/history.jsonl
/target
eval/agent/results/
# Written by `vexus init --agent claude-code` for local dogfooding — machine-
# local MCP wiring; every contributor generates their own.
.mcp.json
# Agent-local settings and steering-pack files that `vexus init` (and agent
# CLIs themselves) create in a checkout — per-machine, never shared.
.claude/
